course: dictionary
lesson: 10828
title: Velvety and the senses
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Velvety is a describing word. It tells you how something feels, looks or sounds. Velvet is a soft, smooth cloth, so velvety means soft and smooth like velvet.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «Owl wing feathers have comb-like front edges, soft fringes and a velvety surface that muffle the sound of flying.» Muffle means make quieter, so a surface that quietens sound must be soft and smooth, not rough. Swap in soft and smooth, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word can describe more than touch. A velvety voice or a velvety taste is smooth, deep and rich. Ask yourself what is being described: a feeling, a sound, a sight or a taste?
fact: Velvety means soft and smooth like velvet cloth.
fact: «Velvety petals» are soft and smooth to touch.
fact: A velvety voice or taste is smooth, deep and rich.
fact: A European mole has «velvety black fur» that lies flat whichever way it is brushed.
fact: Owl feathers have «a velvety surface» that helps them fly almost silently.
exercise: «Owl wing feathers have a velvety surface that muffle the sound of flying.» What does velvety mean here? | *Soft and smooth | Loud and noisy | Wet and cold | Hard and bumpy
exercise: Leo says velvety must mean sticky. What does velvety really mean? | Sticky and wet | Very loud | *Soft and smooth like velvet cloth | Cold as ice
exercise: «A European mole has velvety black fur that lies flat whichever way it is brushed.» Find and copy the word that describes the fur. | tunnels | *velvety | forwards | European
test: «The velvety moss felt cool under her hand.» What does velvety tell you about the moss? | Slippery like ice | Very hot | Hard as rock | *Soft and smooth to touch
test: «Her velvety voice made the story sound warm.» What does velvety suggest about her voice? | Cold and sharp | Squeaky and thin | Loud and shouting | *Smooth, deep and rich
exam: «Ella sipped the velvety hot chocolate.» What does velvety mean here? | Crunchy | Icy cold | *Smooth and rich | Burnt and bitter
